@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.825 = private unnamed_addr constant [618 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports that are typically imported using a common convention,\0Alike `import pandas as pd`, and enforces that convention.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AConsistency is good. Use a common convention for imports to make your code\0Amore readable and idiomatic.\0A\0AFor example, `import pandas as pd` is a common\0Aconvention for importing the `pandas` library, and users typically expect\0APandas to be aliased as `pd`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-import-conventions.aliases`\0A- `lint.flake8-import-conventions.extend-aliases`\0A", align 1
